{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfgE7n2dVEKQbubx1tJUi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passes the admission self-check (it printed `OK`), but its smoke-fit score is poor and its score estimate is unreliable. It scored an ELPD-LOO of −3782, against −3414 for the current best model. That was a short single-chain run, so it isn't a fair comparison, but the gap is large. About 7% of trials (528 of 7680) were flagged as unreliable for the LOO estimate (high Pareto k), well above the 1% the pipeline accepts. If that holds up in the full fit, the model's score won't count as trusted.\n\nThe self-check doesn't test convergence, novelty against the other models, or the 30-minute fit limit, so those are still open.\n\n**Model name:** `shared_impression_personal_decisiveness`\n\n**Hypothesis:** Everyone forms the same impression of what looks random. That impression uses the same cues as the current best model: how far the running heads-minus-tails tally swings, closeness to an ideal switching rate, variety of three-flip chunks, and a penalty for sequences built by a simple rule. People differ only in how consistently they act on that impression. Each person has one decisiveness gain that multiplies the whole felt difference between the two sequences, plus a personal left/right lean.\n\n**Why this one:** The critique of the best model found one discrepancy that survived the false-discovery correction (q = 0.048). People differ more than the model allows in how often they agree with the majority choice on each pair. The best model lets people differ on separate cues; this one tests the opposite claim. People share what randomness looks like, and the differences between them are in decision noise.\n\nThe files are in `.../experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4036,"cache_read_input_tokens":77057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4036,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96b1ff60-686f-4103-8d13-dd65371c76a8","uuid":"bee0571e-1dc8-4f23-b5a7-02829c213a3a","timestamp":"2026-10-04T00:10:45.554Z","request_id":"req_011CfgE7mf3puxnXUsKujCGT"}
